A||||4||JD||Front End Upgrade 84-87
Z||000000||JD||01-14-99||08:15 AM||||I understand that the front springs on a 84 fiero is different than <br>subsequent years. Could you use the front springs off of an 86 SE into <br>an 84?I am also wondering where you can buy the stiffest springs for the <br>1984 fiero as coded below:<br>1984 10029670 DMF 10029675 DMN (Stiffest) <p>And what aftermarket (more racy springs) you would recommend for the <br>front? Thank you.<br>
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||01-16-99||03:51 PM||||I'll try to find out if the springs of an 86 can be used in a 84. I suspect they can but I'll check to make sure.<p>I've lowered my 86.6 GT to about 3" above the ground and it did wonders for its high-speed stability. It used to drift all over the place! That's almost completely gone now.
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||01-29-99||11:13 AM||||I just got word from Barry from the Fiero Factory in Holland ( <A HREF="http://www.fierofactory.nl" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierofactory.nl</A> ) about the springs:<p><i>There is indeed one type of springs used on the '84 which are *higher* than all subsequent types. Other than the height there is no apparant difference so you should be able to use the springs of an '86 on an '84</i><p>Hope this helps.
Z||000003||raceknb||03-01-99||09:03 PM||||If you check out the Fiero Store catalog, you will see there is an extensive amount of suspension products.  The best thing I can recomend is a good set of springs and poly out the chassis.  Ride is a bit harsh, but will stick like it is on rails...
Z||000004||Tyler||03-11-99||10:02 AM||||I heard from someone (I can't remember who now...) that the springs from an '84SE with the WS6 option were about 1/2" lower than the rest of the years with the WS6 option.  Can anyone out there confirm this?
